802	/**
803	 * The wizard's stored scan snapshot (`Migration.items.scan`) is trimmed on the
804	 * way into the DB and is taken hours or days before the cutover, so it cannot
805	 * answer the questions that decide whether the site actually SERVES afterwards:
806	 * which images back each container, the full `docker inspect` shape of the
807	 * standalone ones, which MySQL accounts the apps log in as, which domains the
808	 * web server answers on, what cron/TLS/system-user state exists.
809	 *
810	 * So the engine re-probes the source itself, live, over the SSH channel it
811	 * already holds. The probe is ONE fixed, code-authored POSIX-sh script that is
812	 * written to the TARGET over SFTP (0600, bytes — never a shell argument) and fed
813	 * to the source with `ssh … sh -s < script`. Travelling on STDIN instead of argv
814	 * means the script needs no quoting gymnastics and contains ZERO interpolated
815	 * values other than a compile-time-constant `sudo -n` prefix, so it has no
816	 * injection surface at all. It is strictly read-only: `docker inspect`, `mysql
817	 * -e SELECT`, `grep`, `ls`, `awk` over /etc/passwd, `du`.
818	 *
819	 * EVERYTHING it returns is untrusted and is re-validated against the allowlists
820	 * above before it can reach any command.
821	 */
